  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "OpenAI expects models to cross the High cybersecurity threshold in the near future.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "3",
        "pdfPage": 4,
        "quote": "We expect current\ntrends of rapidly increasing capability to continue, and for models to cross the High cybersecurity\nthreshold in the near future."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Conversational disallowed-content evals are reported for ecosystem insight; the model is not intended for general-purpose chat.", "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "3",
        "pdfPage": 4,
        "quote": "The model is not intended\nfor deployment in any general-purpose chat application, and will not be deployed by OpenAI in\nany such context."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "GPT-5.1-Codex-Max is the most cyber-capable model OpenAI has deployed to date, aided by compaction across context windows.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "12",
        "pdfPage": 13,
        "quote": "GPT-5.1-\nCodex-Max is the most cyber-capable model we’ve deployed to date."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Cyber Range: solves most scenarios including new ones; fails Medium C2+privilege escalation; Leaked Token only PARTIAL via unintended misconfiguration.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "17",
        "pdfPage": 18,
        "quote": "GPT-5.1-Codex-Max surpasses the performance of all previous models and solves most of the\nscenarios except for the most sophisticated scenario of command-control combined with privilege"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Irregular: similar or slightly reduced cyberoffensive capability vs GPT-5; solved no hard challenges.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "18",
        "pdfPage": 19,
        "quote": "when compared to GPT-5,\nGPT-5.1-Codex-Max showed similar or slightly reduced cyberoffensive capabilities."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Apollo: scheming capability/propensity comparable to GPT-5; likely not capable of catastrophic harm via scheming.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "26",
        "pdfPage": 27,
        "quote": "Based\non these findings, they believe GPT-5.1-Codex-Max is likely not capable of causing catastrophic\nharm via scheming."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "METR: capabilities on-trend; further development unlikely to enable key autonomy threat models in the next 6 months absent a trend break.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "24",
        "pdfPage": 25,
        "quote": "absent a significant trend break, further development would be unlikely to enable these\nthreat models in the next 6 months, based on the following:"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Mental health Production Benchmark not_unsafe falls vs gpt-5.1-thinking (0.52 vs 0.68).", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "4",
        "pdfPage": 5,
        "quote": "              mental health              0.684                   0.519"
      }
    }
  ],
